{
  "round": 4,
  "note": "Round 4 adds the communities where PMs, designers and marketers talk about their work: r/ProductManagement, r/UXDesign, r/userexperience and r/marketing. Same two-year window as Hacker News. Same search terms as round 2 so the sources can be compared, except 'feedback loop' (almost all noise in round 2) and two broad terms that fit non-engineers' wording: 'dev team' and 'stakeholders'. No terms were added for any hypothesis or candidate product (H6, review and approval flow, Blast Radius). For each post that really contains its term, the top 30 comments come too, since that's where people describe their own experience. Comments are kept as part of the thread and don't need to contain the term.",
